1
00:00:06,603 --> 00:00:08,336
[Episode 11]

2
00:00:13,470 --> 00:00:15,170
Why are you...

3
00:00:18,570 --> 00:00:20,070
Halt!

4
00:00:21,870 --> 00:00:23,436
Identify yourselves.

5
00:00:26,570 --> 00:00:28,403
Unhand her.

6
00:00:31,236 --> 00:00:32,570
I said unhand her.

7
00:00:33,470 --> 00:00:35,236
My Lord.

8
00:00:36,136 --> 00:00:40,103
Are you deaf?
Unhand her now!

9
00:00:41,636 --> 00:00:43,303
Get them!

10
00:01:03,303 --> 00:01:07,503
Back away or I'll cut her.

11
00:01:08,536 --> 00:01:13,270
- My Lord.
- Stop this or we'll stop you.

12
00:01:13,270 --> 00:01:15,136
Now!

13
00:01:36,570 --> 00:01:39,570
- Are you alright?
- My Lord.

14
00:01:39,636 --> 00:01:44,070
What are you doing here
at this time of night?

15
00:01:53,603 --> 00:01:55,470
Your orders, Sir?

16
00:01:55,562 --> 00:02:02,526
They look like common criminals.
Hand them over to the local police.

17
00:02:02,636 --> 00:02:04,489
Sir.

18
00:02:14,136 --> 00:02:15,753
The King's not in the palace?

19
00:02:15,936 --> 00:02:20,399
No. He was looking for you
at the Police Bureau.

20
00:02:22,070 --> 00:02:23,370
What?

21
00:02:23,370 --> 00:02:26,336
Well? What were you doing here?

22
00:02:27,170 --> 00:02:30,203
Thank you, My Lord.
You saved my life.

23
00:02:30,270 --> 00:02:33,103
What have I told you?
Go out early.

24
00:02:33,203 --> 00:02:36,670
If I hadn't come by,
who knows what might have happened.

25
00:02:37,136 --> 00:02:42,570
I'm sorry, My Lord,
but this was especially important.

26
00:02:44,270 --> 00:02:45,536
Especially?

27
00:02:45,570 --> 00:02:49,403
I was looking for you, actually.

28
00:02:50,070 --> 00:02:52,103
For me?

29
00:02:52,270 --> 00:02:53,436
For me? Why?

30
00:02:53,470 --> 00:02:57,470
I had to tell you something.
I went to the administrative offices.

31
00:02:57,470 --> 00:02:59,270
You what?

32
00:03:00,036 --> 00:03:06,136
But the guard said
you'd never heard of me.

33
00:03:08,270 --> 00:03:13,603
Why'd you say that, though?

34
00:03:15,136 --> 00:03:18,336
I'm not sure...

35
00:03:18,403 --> 00:03:23,170
Wait! The guard went to Officer Kang,
of course. That's it.

36
00:03:23,170 --> 00:03:24,636
Huh?

37
00:03:24,636 --> 00:03:27,470
There are two inspectors in our office.
Kang's the other one.

38
00:03:27,603 --> 00:03:32,370
- Ah, so that's it?
- Of course. I'd never say that.

39
00:03:32,403 --> 00:03:37,403
Ah, I see. I thought maybe
you'd forgotten me.

40
00:03:38,670 --> 00:03:43,170
So what was so important that
you had to come find me?

41
00:03:44,203 --> 00:03:46,136
Well, it's this way...

42
00:03:52,470 --> 00:03:55,636
What?
The King saved her?

43
00:03:55,636 --> 00:04:01,270
Yes, Sir. The royal guard turned
them over to the local police.

44
00:04:07,336 --> 00:04:12,703
Luckily they're being tried as
common criminals. We're safe on that score.

45
00:04:14,403 --> 00:04:23,570
But what went wrong? The King saving
a servant? Why would he do that?

46
00:04:32,670 --> 00:04:34,170
Sire.

47
00:04:35,303 --> 00:04:36,670
Sire.

48
00:04:40,070 --> 00:04:42,636
I spoke with the girl on the way here.

49
00:04:43,203 --> 00:04:46,236
Do we really have information
that clears Lady Jang?

50
00:04:47,203 --> 00:04:49,170
Yes, Sire.

51
00:04:50,236 --> 00:04:53,370
Where's the body?
I need to see it.

52
00:04:53,436 --> 00:04:55,270
Sire.

53
00:05:19,570 --> 00:05:22,370
- Show His Highness.
- Sir.

54
00:05:26,503 --> 00:05:30,436
- Now with some pinellia on your hands.
- Sir.

55
00:05:52,103 --> 00:05:55,403
But... How could...

56
00:05:56,570 --> 00:06:02,636
Contact with pinellia would have
discolored the doctor's hands.

57
00:06:03,636 --> 00:06:05,670
That's what happened, Sire.

58
00:06:06,170 --> 00:06:12,136
This proves the pharmacist
didn't send pinellia to Lady Jang.

59
00:06:16,503 --> 00:06:21,270
And Dongyi discovered this?

60
00:06:21,336 --> 00:06:23,703
Yes, Sire.

61
00:06:23,703 --> 00:06:26,270
Someone murdered the doctor
over an old grudge.

62
00:06:26,270 --> 00:06:35,503
We made the arrest and failed
to examine the corpses carefully.

63
00:06:38,470 --> 00:06:44,136
She saw what hundreds officers missed.

64
00:07:19,570 --> 00:07:22,403
Is everything ready for the inquisitors?

65
00:07:22,403 --> 00:07:24,336
Yes.

66
00:07:24,336 --> 00:07:30,536
They'll be here soon. You understand
we can't let this tarnish our reputation?

67
00:07:30,570 --> 00:07:32,703
Yes, My Lady.

68
00:07:41,436 --> 00:07:50,136
You've done well. You can all expect
a reward for such a satisfactory conclusion.

69
00:07:52,603 --> 00:07:55,670
With special thanks to Lady Yu.

70
00:07:56,370 --> 00:07:57,636
Not at all.

71
00:07:58,503 --> 00:08:03,503
When this is over we'll pay
a visit to the Queen Mother.

72
00:08:03,770 --> 00:08:05,503
Ma'am?

73
00:08:05,570 --> 00:08:10,403
She'd like to thank us for our work
with the inspectorate.

74
00:08:10,436 --> 00:08:13,603
Just as you say. I'll be waiting.

75
00:08:20,570 --> 00:08:27,503
That's wonderful.
An audience with the Queen!

76
00:08:28,270 --> 00:08:33,503
You're bound to be the next
Lady Inspector General.

77
00:08:33,570 --> 00:08:37,203
Don't get ahead of yourself.
It's not over yet.

78
00:08:37,203 --> 00:08:39,236
Yes, ma'am.

79
00:08:43,703 --> 00:08:46,336
These are our prescription records.

80
00:08:47,336 --> 00:08:51,170
- May I have this?
- Of course.

81
00:08:59,303 --> 00:09:06,203
I picked up the prescription myself.
I'm certain there was no pinellia, My Lady.

82
00:09:07,603 --> 00:09:11,503
- Sanghi!
- What did you learn?

83
00:09:11,603 --> 00:09:14,136
The girl was right.

84
00:09:14,136 --> 00:09:17,736
None of the usual vendors
supplied pinellia to that pharmacy.

85
00:09:17,736 --> 00:09:19,270
None?

86
00:09:33,203 --> 00:09:40,236
Well, Your Highness?
Will you accept this small token?

87
00:09:42,270 --> 00:09:49,536
If so, you can rest easy.
We can finally put this behind us.

88
00:09:50,303 --> 00:09:56,170
I'll be much relieved.

89
00:09:57,636 --> 00:10:03,336
Impudent little... Do you think
your influence will last forever?

90
00:10:03,436 --> 00:10:05,303
Lady Do to see you.

91
00:10:11,403 --> 00:10:14,070
- You asked for me, Your Highness?
- Yes.

92
00:10:14,136 --> 00:10:16,570
Prepare my things for a short visit.

93
00:10:17,170 --> 00:10:19,103
Where to, Your Highness?

94
00:10:19,103 --> 00:10:22,570
Lady Jang is being transferred
to the inquisitors.

95
00:10:23,270 --> 00:10:28,203
It's only fitting I see her off.

96
00:10:33,503 --> 00:10:37,470
What's that?
Reopen the case?

97
00:10:37,570 --> 00:10:43,636
None of the vendors supplied this
dead pharmacist with the pinellia.

98
00:10:44,036 --> 00:10:45,036
Pardon?

99
00:10:45,303 --> 00:10:47,036
Lady Jung was right.

100
00:10:47,036 --> 00:10:53,636
The vendors stopped supplying it
after someone died from pinellia.

101
00:10:53,636 --> 00:10:56,570
The girl from the royal
musiciangs office was right.

102
00:10:56,636 --> 00:11:00,503
- We should give the inquisitors the facts.
- Facts?

103
00:11:00,536 --> 00:11:02,436
What facts are those?

104
00:11:02,536 --> 00:11:04,103
- Your Ladyship.
- Your Ladyship.

105
00:11:04,170 --> 00:11:07,603
Just because there's no record
doesn't mean he never used it.

106
00:11:07,636 --> 00:11:10,436
He may have bought
the pinellia in secret.

107
00:11:10,436 --> 00:11:13,136
- But...
- Enough of your buts!

108
00:11:13,170 --> 00:11:18,503
The pinellia was in Lady Jang's chambers.
What other proof do we need?

109
00:11:18,536 --> 00:11:25,070
My Lady... My Lady...
It's just awful! Come quick!

110
00:11:52,603 --> 00:11:58,503
Wait... Isn't that the palace guard?
Where are the inquisitors?

111
00:12:01,203 --> 00:12:07,503
They didn't come to transfer Lady Jang.
They came to protect her.

112
00:12:07,503 --> 00:12:09,603
- Huh?
- What?

113
00:12:30,570 --> 00:12:34,236
She was scheduled to be transferred
at 8 a.m., isn't that right?

114
00:12:34,236 --> 00:12:37,236
So I understand.

115
00:12:37,336 --> 00:12:39,203
Find out what happened.

116
00:12:39,203 --> 00:12:41,103
- Of course.
- Your Highness...

117
00:12:41,103 --> 00:12:43,103
Oh, it's unheard of!

118
00:12:43,203 --> 00:12:45,470
What's unheard of?

119
00:12:46,103 --> 00:12:51,070
The King has rescinded Lady Jang's
transfer to the inquisitors.

120
00:12:52,170 --> 00:12:55,303
What's that? On what grounds?

121
00:13:02,036 --> 00:13:05,203
Innocent? It's impossible.

122
00:13:05,203 --> 00:13:07,136
- The facts were...
- Facts?

123
00:13:07,236 --> 00:13:09,370
Here are your facts!

124
00:13:10,136 --> 00:13:14,603
Straight from the Police Bureau.
It proves she's innocent.

125
00:13:15,103 --> 00:13:18,303
The King confirmed the facts himself.

126
00:13:25,170 --> 00:13:29,303
Who do you think uncovered the facts?
A girl from the Office of Royal Musicians.

127
00:13:29,303 --> 00:13:31,170
Pardon?

128
00:13:31,170 --> 00:13:35,070
Do you see now?
What you couldn't see

129
00:13:35,070 --> 00:13:39,336
in your haste was perfectly clear
to a simple servant girl.

130
00:13:39,336 --> 00:13:43,236
Now what? Who will bear
the brunt of this disgrace?

131
00:13:56,570 --> 00:14:00,503
Wait here. We'll have
a few questions for you.

132
00:14:01,103 --> 00:14:02,503
Yes, Sir.

133
00:14:15,536 --> 00:14:17,470
That's the one.

134
00:14:17,470 --> 00:14:22,136
That wisp of a girl proved
Lady Jang is innocent?

135
00:14:22,270 --> 00:14:23,670
So I'm told.

136
00:14:32,436 --> 00:14:37,470
Dongyi cleared my name?

137
00:14:37,470 --> 00:14:39,370
She did indeed.

138
00:14:41,336 --> 00:14:45,236
You've been unjustly accused.

139
00:14:45,236 --> 00:14:52,436
The King commands that Lady Jang
be given full royal escort to her home.

140
00:15:14,270 --> 00:15:16,370
- My Lady.
- My Lady.

141
00:15:17,703 --> 00:15:20,436
This must have been difficult for you.

142
00:15:20,436 --> 00:15:24,336
What does that matter?

143
00:15:24,336 --> 00:15:30,236
We're beside ourselves knowing
you were so unjustly accused.

144
00:15:31,436 --> 00:15:33,436
We beg your forgiveness.

145
00:15:33,436 --> 00:15:39,636
I doubt we can ever be free
of this terrible disgrace.

146
00:15:42,670 --> 00:15:46,503
Well? Beg the lady for forgiveness.

147
00:15:47,503 --> 00:15:53,536
Forgive us.
We were entirely in the wrong.

148
00:15:53,536 --> 00:15:58,203
We throw ourselves at your mercy.

149
00:16:06,236 --> 00:16:13,703
Actually, you shouldn't
be apologizing to me.

150
00:16:13,703 --> 00:16:19,103
Ask forgiveness of the servant girl
that saw clearer than you.

151
00:16:20,670 --> 00:16:28,636
She learned the truth despite
all of you. Isn't that right?

152
00:16:39,470 --> 00:16:45,303
Well, Lady Yu? When you're
no better than a servant girl.

153
00:16:45,303 --> 00:16:52,170
It makes me fear for the future
of the Inspector General.

154
00:16:57,570 --> 00:17:00,270
Well? Make way for the lady.

155
00:17:42,403 --> 00:17:46,103
Bring me Dongyi.
She's the first one I want to see.

156
00:17:46,103 --> 00:17:48,170
As you say.

157
00:17:55,636 --> 00:17:58,503
Ma'am, please try to relax.

158
00:17:59,403 --> 00:18:05,303
A musician? I'm disgraced
because of a servant?

159
00:18:11,603 --> 00:18:15,270
The world's turned upside down, I swear.

160
00:18:16,170 --> 00:18:21,236
When a musician can do this to us?
Our reputationgs shot.

161
00:18:21,236 --> 00:18:26,636
That's my point. Everybody's heard
about it. We'll be a joke.

162
00:18:26,636 --> 00:18:32,203
She's nothing. Even napping fishermen
catch something if the net's big enough.

163
00:18:32,203 --> 00:18:37,436
What about you? Did you even
bother tossing out a net?

164
00:18:38,236 --> 00:18:39,603
Ma'am.

165
00:18:40,570 --> 00:18:45,570
Little twits. You think you have
any right to be angry?

166
00:18:45,570 --> 00:18:50,470
If you don't like it,
apply yourselves harder next time.

167
00:18:54,336 --> 00:18:57,603
Well? Are you still here?

168
00:19:02,670 --> 00:19:08,636
I don't understand.
How did a servant think of it?

169
00:19:08,703 --> 00:19:12,270
Good point.
I'm surprised too.

170
00:19:13,236 --> 00:19:18,136
You two discovered facts.
You should mention...

171
00:19:18,170 --> 00:19:21,603
It would only sound like excuses.

172
00:19:23,203 --> 00:19:28,370
Making excuses is worse than making
a mistake in the first place.

173
00:19:28,470 --> 00:19:31,670
We were clearly mistaken.

174
00:19:31,703 --> 00:19:36,270
None of us was as clever as
this servant girl.

175
00:19:48,403 --> 00:19:52,270
- Lady Jo reporting.
- Enter.

176
00:19:54,636 --> 00:19:57,636
Dongyi is with me.

177
00:19:57,670 --> 00:19:59,570
Send her in.

178
00:20:00,336 --> 00:20:02,303
Enter.

179
00:20:07,336 --> 00:20:08,536
Welcome.

180
00:20:08,670 --> 00:20:10,470
My Lady.

181
00:20:12,203 --> 00:20:15,670
- Have a seat.
- Thank you.

182
00:20:21,336 --> 00:20:33,403
I'm at a loss. No words can express
my gratitude.

183
00:20:34,136 --> 00:20:42,536
Not at all. It's nothing compared to the
grace and kindness you've shown me.

184
00:20:42,636 --> 00:20:45,170
Nothing, you say?

185
00:20:45,270 --> 00:20:51,536
I'm returned safely to my home
and you call it nothing?

186
00:20:51,570 --> 00:20:53,336
My Lady...

187
00:20:53,370 --> 00:20:59,503
I knew you're a gifted girl
but I confess I'm surprised.

188
00:20:59,536 --> 00:21:03,636
What made you think of it?

189
00:21:04,570 --> 00:21:08,503
It... It was faith.

190
00:21:09,503 --> 00:21:10,636
Pardon?

191
00:21:10,670 --> 00:21:15,303
Faith that you couldn't
possibly have done it.

192
00:21:15,336 --> 00:21:23,436
Faith that there had to be proof,
that the body would reveal the truth.

193
00:21:24,670 --> 00:21:28,670
What I did was nothing.

194
00:21:28,670 --> 00:21:38,103
I'm nothing. I don't know where I'd be
if you hadn't shown me such kindness.

195
00:21:44,270 --> 00:21:45,636
You're wrong.

196
00:21:46,503 --> 00:21:51,303
You're a clever girl,
but today you're wrong.

197
00:21:52,370 --> 00:21:54,036
My Lady?

198
00:21:55,103 --> 00:21:59,536
You're nothing? No.

199
00:21:59,570 --> 00:22:05,170
To me... You're very precious indeed.

200
00:22:06,570 --> 00:22:08,670
My Lady.

201
00:22:15,370 --> 00:22:17,636
Here we go again.

202
00:22:19,103 --> 00:22:25,370
Lady Jang unjustly imprisoned and
her accuser has disappeared.

203
00:22:27,170 --> 00:22:33,070
Worse, it's less than a month since
this happened the last time.

204
00:22:34,603 --> 00:22:40,136
You see this is what's wrong with
our current system, don't you?

205
00:22:40,203 --> 00:22:49,103
What bothers me isn't Lady Jang,
it's our entire government.

206
00:22:52,470 --> 00:22:57,436
This is all due to your political infighting,
your power plays and endless slander.

207
00:22:58,103 --> 00:23:07,703
We're destroying ourselves from
the inside and don't even know it.

208
00:23:08,436 --> 00:23:10,703
Forgive us, Sire.

209
00:23:12,670 --> 00:23:19,736
It's my fault for thinking you could
control yourselves.

210
00:23:19,736 --> 00:23:22,536
Now you will listen to your King.

211
00:23:23,503 --> 00:23:28,470
This will not be forgiven again.

212
00:23:29,236 --> 00:23:32,536
I will find the one behind this.

213
00:23:33,536 --> 00:23:39,236
And whoever it is, I will show no mercy.
Is that understood?

214
00:23:40,403 --> 00:23:43,336
Forgive us, Sire.

215
00:23:51,203 --> 00:23:53,636
Actually, I'm the most to blame.

216
00:23:55,136 --> 00:24:00,336
Didn't I say it was politics
to overlook their crimes?

217
00:24:01,436 --> 00:24:10,270
It bothered you when I asked you
to look the other way, didn't it?

218
00:24:11,403 --> 00:24:14,436
Well... That is...

219
00:24:15,303 --> 00:24:18,436
It's not your way to be a sycophant.

220
00:24:18,436 --> 00:24:20,436
Forgive me, Sire.

221
00:24:21,270 --> 00:24:27,636
But the days of looking
the other way are over.

222
00:24:27,636 --> 00:24:29,670
I want you to help me
find the one behind this.

223
00:24:31,270 --> 00:24:34,636
It won't be easy.
And it won't be quick.

224
00:24:35,136 --> 00:24:39,236
And the instigator may be
too highly placed.

225
00:24:40,536 --> 00:24:45,403
But I know you'll never stop,
whoever it is.

226
00:24:46,403 --> 00:24:50,370
Remember what I've said.
Be thorough.

227
00:24:51,370 --> 00:24:55,136
I will give it my full attention, Sire.

228
00:25:03,703 --> 00:25:06,370
What's taking Dongyi so long?

229
00:25:07,136 --> 00:25:11,536
Lady Jang's probably giving her
some fancy reward...

230
00:25:11,536 --> 00:25:14,536
Better yet...

231
00:25:15,270 --> 00:25:21,236
A banquet. Chances are
it's another royal banquet.

232
00:25:21,270 --> 00:25:23,370
Huh? Another one?

233
00:25:25,270 --> 00:25:28,336
I thought she'd lost it when she said
she had to yak with a corpse.

234
00:25:28,336 --> 00:25:31,303
But look at her now!

235
00:25:31,336 --> 00:25:33,536
And me, if I'd only known...

236
00:25:33,603 --> 00:25:37,370
I would've trotted after her and joined
in the conversation.

237
00:25:39,303 --> 00:25:40,636
Dongyi!

238
00:25:41,203 --> 00:25:43,570
Dongyi!

239
00:25:51,403 --> 00:25:54,336
What's going on?

240
00:25:54,370 --> 00:25:57,403
What did you get?
Show us!

241
00:25:57,503 --> 00:26:01,536
What are you doing?
Hands off.

242
00:26:03,603 --> 00:26:07,236
Gold? Silk? Some cash maybe?

243
00:26:07,336 --> 00:26:09,303
No, it's just...

244
00:26:11,236 --> 00:26:15,436
- Ugh.
- Stinky...

245
00:26:17,203 --> 00:26:19,503
What the? Boots?

246
00:26:21,670 --> 00:26:24,270
Why are these things in here?

247
00:26:25,303 --> 00:26:30,236
Lord Jang told me to clean
and mend them.

248
00:26:31,236 --> 00:26:34,636
So you didn't get no reward or nothing?

249
00:26:34,636 --> 00:26:36,336
Reward?

250
00:26:36,336 --> 00:26:40,636
Yeah reward. She really didn't
give you nothing?

251
00:26:41,470 --> 00:26:44,336
Right. Nothing.

252
00:26:52,536 --> 00:26:54,170
Sir...

253
00:27:01,570 --> 00:27:05,703
Why are you all?

254
00:27:05,703 --> 00:27:09,370
Ah, so you thought this was a reward?

255
00:27:09,436 --> 00:27:16,536
Well Yeah. Big doings earn big rewards
like a banquet maybe?

256
00:27:16,536 --> 00:27:19,703
Come on, I didn't do it for a reward.

257
00:27:20,703 --> 00:27:25,436
Hush, hush! Maybe you didn't...
but what about the King?

258
00:27:25,503 --> 00:27:29,370
You saved his Lady Jang yet again.

259
00:27:29,370 --> 00:27:33,370
All the same...
We're probably acting too soon.

260
00:27:33,370 --> 00:27:37,403
Last time the banquet was the following day,
so we should wait.

261
00:27:38,170 --> 00:27:43,403
Right. It takes a day
to prepare the feast, at least.

262
00:27:44,636 --> 00:27:48,636
How will you feel
when they don't make anything?

263
00:27:49,170 --> 00:27:51,136
That's not going to happen.

264
00:27:53,436 --> 00:27:56,170
Think we'll get the steamed fish?

265
00:27:56,170 --> 00:28:00,636
You like that?
Me, I like the grilled beef.

266
00:28:02,236 --> 00:28:04,736
I'll starve myself tonight.

267
00:28:04,736 --> 00:28:08,403
Good thinking.
We won't eat nothing.

268
00:28:09,303 --> 00:28:11,503
But...

269
00:28:12,336 --> 00:28:14,536
Your fish, Sir...

270
00:28:18,303 --> 00:28:20,370
Come on, quick, give it here...

271
00:28:20,403 --> 00:28:22,170
Your beef, Sir...

272
00:28:26,570 --> 00:28:30,236
What's got into them, I swear...

273
00:28:47,603 --> 00:28:50,503
You sent the medicines to Lady Jang?

274
00:28:50,503 --> 00:28:58,170
I did, but may I ask why?
When I think about her conduct...

275
00:28:58,170 --> 00:29:01,370
Let's have no more of that.

276
00:29:02,536 --> 00:29:06,536
She went through enough over my tonic.

277
00:29:06,536 --> 00:29:07,470
Your Majesty.

278
00:29:08,536 --> 00:29:10,603
You gave her my compliments?

279
00:29:11,503 --> 00:29:16,736
I didn't see her in person.
The King was with her.

280
00:29:17,303 --> 00:29:19,503
- Was he?
- He was.

281
00:29:22,336 --> 00:29:26,536
I understand a servant girl from
the musicians saved the lady.

282
00:29:26,636 --> 00:29:30,503
So I understand as well.

283
00:29:31,670 --> 00:29:37,503
Even Lady Jang's servants are remarkable.

284
00:29:38,703 --> 00:29:44,603
I find myself a little jealous of her.

285
00:29:45,470 --> 00:29:47,270
Your Majesty.

286
00:30:01,503 --> 00:30:04,203
Were you terribly upset with me?

287
00:30:06,136 --> 00:30:14,070
I already told you.
Just seeing you makes it all better.

288
00:30:17,070 --> 00:30:20,536
Thank you for saying so.

289
00:30:22,570 --> 00:30:26,636
We owe a lot to this Dongyi of yours.

290
00:30:30,436 --> 00:30:38,403
When I think a simple servant girl...
Well, it's surprising to say the least.

291
00:30:38,403 --> 00:30:43,103
Yes, Sire. Very much so.

292
00:30:44,136 --> 00:30:50,336
I think her talents are wasted running
errands for the royal musicians.

293
00:30:52,503 --> 00:30:59,103
Sire, if I may beg a favor?

294
00:30:59,170 --> 00:31:02,536
A favor? For her?

295
00:31:03,336 --> 00:31:05,336
Yes, Sire.

296
00:31:13,370 --> 00:31:16,570
Go easy.
No need to strain anything.

297
00:31:16,670 --> 00:31:20,670
I have to catch up on all the stuff
I didn't do yesterday.

298
00:31:21,303 --> 00:31:22,570
Sorry.

299
00:31:23,336 --> 00:31:25,603
All the same you've got a bad lot.

300
00:31:25,670 --> 00:31:28,103
I mean, you do this great thing, right?

301
00:31:28,103 --> 00:31:32,603
And you're still a servant
slaving all day.

302
00:31:34,070 --> 00:31:39,370
Got that right. Someone with your
talent born in a low caste.

303
00:31:40,170 --> 00:31:45,570
If you'd been born a boy, even one level up,
things would be different.

304
00:31:45,636 --> 00:31:51,536
Oh, enough of that.
We all get lucky sometimes.

305
00:31:51,536 --> 00:31:54,136
I'll put this music away.

306
00:31:56,370 --> 00:32:04,436
What good is a caste system when someone
like her is stuck at the bottom?

307
00:32:23,670 --> 00:32:32,570
What good is a caste system when someone
like her is stuck at the bottom?

308
00:32:36,203 --> 00:32:40,603
Moron... what are you thinking?

309
00:33:05,703 --> 00:33:09,270
You really intend to use her?

310
00:33:09,270 --> 00:33:13,403
Yes, if the King permits.

311
00:33:14,236 --> 00:33:18,403
It's an opportunity for her. And for me.

312
00:33:18,503 --> 00:33:22,370
Dongyi is clever enough, I admit...

313
00:33:22,503 --> 00:33:28,503
- But the outcry in the palace...
- That's not for you to say.

314
00:33:29,503 --> 00:33:31,303
Of course.

315
00:33:32,070 --> 00:33:35,236
Oh, do you have news of my Brother?

316
00:33:35,236 --> 00:33:41,436
Yes, he sailed from Qing.
He'll arrive in Doseong soon.

317
00:33:42,203 --> 00:33:45,136
I'd like him to meet Dongyi.

318
00:33:46,103 --> 00:33:52,303
He's good at reading people.
I'd like to see what he makes of her.

319
00:34:14,136 --> 00:34:15,636
Are you heading straight home?

320
00:34:17,103 --> 00:34:21,303
No, I have a few things
to take care of first.

321
00:34:21,303 --> 00:34:23,303
Sir?

322
00:34:23,303 --> 00:34:29,303
I'm going to let this city
know I've returned.

323
00:34:43,336 --> 00:34:45,170
Where is it?

324
00:34:51,370 --> 00:34:55,270
8 a.m., he says.
So where is he?

325
00:34:58,570 --> 00:35:01,470
What if they start the feast without me?

326
00:35:05,470 --> 00:35:08,603
- Excuse me.
- You want a room, right?

327
00:35:08,670 --> 00:35:13,503
- Exactly, I was...
- Good, great, Come on!

328
00:35:14,570 --> 00:35:15,536
Right.

329
00:35:19,136 --> 00:35:25,336
This is it. Nice, huh?
Roomy for the price too.

330
00:35:26,236 --> 00:35:30,736
You know I'm a Royal Musician,
don't you?

331
00:35:30,736 --> 00:35:32,670
So I understood.

332
00:35:33,103 --> 00:35:36,636
I'm the artistic type so I really hate dirt.

333
00:35:37,270 --> 00:35:43,536
Like this for example.
Dirt is so dirty.

334
00:35:44,536 --> 00:35:47,170
I'll keep the room clean.

335
00:35:47,170 --> 00:35:49,236
See that you do.

336
00:35:50,436 --> 00:35:56,403
I'm more of a fighter than a talker,
so just you do what you're told!

337
00:35:58,603 --> 00:36:01,470
- Sound good?
- Of course.

338
00:36:02,070 --> 00:36:05,470
Make yourself at home.
I've got to go do some stuff.

339
00:36:05,470 --> 00:36:07,170
Yes, Sir.

340
00:36:10,703 --> 00:36:16,270
Another court musician of all things,
just like Dongju.

341
00:36:21,503 --> 00:36:23,703
Argh, I'm late!

342
00:36:27,370 --> 00:36:29,703
You... You have to save me...

343
00:36:30,136 --> 00:36:31,403
Me?

344
00:36:32,103 --> 00:36:33,570
Please.

345
00:36:47,203 --> 00:36:49,303
You see someone go in there?

346
00:36:49,303 --> 00:36:53,370
- Someone?
- In there. I saw him.

347
00:36:53,370 --> 00:36:56,136
What the? That's my house.

348
00:36:56,170 --> 00:36:57,336
Move it, turkey.

349
00:36:58,203 --> 00:37:00,403
I got your turkey right here...

350
00:37:00,503 --> 00:37:02,603
Turkey this!

351
00:37:02,603 --> 00:37:05,670
You two in it together, huh?

352
00:37:05,703 --> 00:37:07,370
Save me! Somebody!

353
00:37:07,370 --> 00:37:08,703
Unhand him.

354
00:37:11,336 --> 00:37:15,670
Whatever this is, it's his house.
So hands off.

355
00:37:15,703 --> 00:37:17,336
Another turkey!

356
00:37:24,103 --> 00:37:25,170
Rotten little!

357
00:37:39,336 --> 00:37:41,636
You should get while the getting's good.

358
00:37:46,303 --> 00:37:47,370
Let's git.

359
00:37:47,436 --> 00:37:49,170
No... Don't...

360
00:37:49,170 --> 00:37:50,636
Are you hurt, Sir?

361
00:37:51,336 --> 00:37:54,170
Yeah, great, nothing wrong here.

362
00:37:56,403 --> 00:38:05,736
Whoa, that was really something.
You got a name?

363
00:38:06,470 --> 00:38:08,170
This the man they were chasing?

364
00:38:08,170 --> 00:38:09,403
It is.

365
00:38:10,136 --> 00:38:11,670
What are you up to exactly?

366
00:38:11,670 --> 00:38:16,636
Not much.
Just me and his wife is all.

367
00:38:17,136 --> 00:38:18,636
Huh? Come again?

368
00:38:19,636 --> 00:38:26,670
So his wife wants a little on the side,
nothing for him to worry about.

369
00:38:26,703 --> 00:38:28,236
Don't you think?

370
00:38:37,403 --> 00:38:40,370
I swear, he has no clue what I'm saying...

371
00:38:40,370 --> 00:38:42,603
What? Jang Hijae is back?

372
00:38:43,136 --> 00:38:46,636
And in trouble the second he gets here?

373
00:38:46,670 --> 00:38:51,236
Yes. He had to buy his way
out of a fix yet again.

374
00:38:54,270 --> 00:38:58,636
How did Lady Jang end up
with such a pathetic Brother?

375
00:38:59,503 --> 00:39:04,570
It's nothing to concern yourself with, Sir.
It works out better for us this way.

376
00:39:04,570 --> 00:39:09,470
Wouldn't it be worse if he tried to use
Lady Jang's position to get ahead?

377
00:39:11,136 --> 00:39:17,670
Even so, we should find him a position
where he can't do any harm.

378
00:39:18,436 --> 00:39:20,536
Yes, Sir.

379
00:39:20,536 --> 00:39:23,470
Yeah, he's back today, Father.

380
00:39:23,470 --> 00:39:25,303
Yes!

381
00:39:26,670 --> 00:39:32,403
Uh-oh, now that the womanizer's back
it'll be hard on poor Madam Yun.

382
00:39:33,236 --> 00:39:36,670
Yep. That's a fact.

383
00:39:43,236 --> 00:39:48,470
Now Jang Hijae is here,
I have a friend in Doseong, Father.

384
00:39:48,570 --> 00:39:52,570
Yep, yep, let's have him for a drinks.

385
00:39:52,603 --> 00:39:57,236
- I'll arrange it.
- Yep, yep.

386
00:40:01,136 --> 00:40:07,370
First day back and already
making trouble? When will it end?

387
00:40:07,370 --> 00:40:12,303
True, true.
It makes me sick too.

388
00:40:12,403 --> 00:40:15,670
Huh? Are you making excuses?

389
00:40:16,136 --> 00:40:21,270
- Not at all.
- Hush. I can't stand to look at you.

390
00:40:22,070 --> 00:40:26,136
And a girl from the palace in the house.
It's mortifying.

391
00:40:27,303 --> 00:40:29,603
A girl?

392
00:40:29,603 --> 00:40:35,136
Yes. The servant that saved
your Sister from the inquisitors.

393
00:40:36,503 --> 00:40:39,070
In our house, you say?

394
00:40:40,470 --> 00:40:45,370
Do you have any idea what
your Sister's been through?

395
00:40:46,036 --> 00:40:49,403
Will she ever be able to rely on you?

396
00:40:50,203 --> 00:40:53,070
Where's the girl?

397
00:41:03,236 --> 00:41:05,403
So you're her.

398
00:41:08,470 --> 00:41:10,270
May I ask your name, Sir?

399
00:41:12,503 --> 00:41:15,070
Not a total loss, I'd say.

400
00:41:18,670 --> 00:41:23,503
- Sir, why are you?
- Why? Don't you like it?

401
00:41:24,336 --> 00:41:27,670
Relax. Definitely not my type.

402
00:41:28,503 --> 00:41:29,436
Huh?

403
00:41:29,503 --> 00:41:34,436
Sir, Madam has asked to see her.

404
00:41:35,103 --> 00:41:38,536
Off with you.
She's asking for you.

405
00:41:39,236 --> 00:41:41,170
Yes, Sir.

406
00:41:56,536 --> 00:41:58,070
Hijae.

407
00:42:02,036 --> 00:42:03,270
Your Ladyship.

408
00:42:04,103 --> 00:42:05,436
When did you get here?

409
00:42:05,603 --> 00:42:10,103
Today. I rushed here
the second we landed.

410
00:42:21,370 --> 00:42:25,203
I've been waiting for you to come back.

411
00:42:25,236 --> 00:42:31,536
Yes, me too.
Waiting and yearning.

412
00:42:31,536 --> 00:42:37,270
Is that why you misbehaved
the second you landed?

413
00:42:39,603 --> 00:42:44,603
You heard, huh?
Yes, you would have.

414
00:42:44,603 --> 00:42:52,470
I need people to think of me
as a womanizer and a loafer.

415
00:42:52,503 --> 00:42:55,203
They won't watch me as closely.

416
00:42:55,203 --> 00:42:58,536
- Hijae...
- The time isn't right.

417
00:42:58,536 --> 00:43:04,370
This idleness is killing me
but it's not time yet.

418
00:43:04,370 --> 00:43:07,103
No, it's time, Hijae.

419
00:43:08,403 --> 00:43:13,436
Do you recall my oath
when I first came to the palace?

420
00:43:15,170 --> 00:43:22,470
I swore I'd gain the highest position
I could, remember?

421
00:43:25,103 --> 00:43:27,636
Our days of watching are over.

422
00:43:27,670 --> 00:43:33,570
Now we walk the path we've waited
for so long.

423
00:43:34,303 --> 00:43:38,236
There can be no hesitation
once this starts.

424
00:43:38,236 --> 00:43:40,570
I agree.

425
00:43:41,503 --> 00:43:46,436
I've been helped by a young girl.
She's clever and trustworthy.

426
00:43:47,570 --> 00:43:53,603
She'll be the stone that makes waves
in the calm of the inner court.

427
00:43:54,103 --> 00:43:58,470
The servant from the Office
of Royal Musicians?

428
00:43:59,236 --> 00:44:01,636
You've heard about her?

429
00:44:01,636 --> 00:44:05,270
Heard and seen, I dare say.

430
00:44:05,270 --> 00:44:09,103
- You met her?
- Yes.

431
00:44:10,303 --> 00:44:16,536
And? I value your impressions
above all others.

432
00:44:19,570 --> 00:44:24,436
What is it? Didn't you like her?

433
00:44:28,103 --> 00:44:29,470
Hijae.

434
00:44:29,503 --> 00:44:34,670
I can see what you like about her,
really I can.

435
00:44:35,370 --> 00:44:40,236
But I don't think I'd keep her too close.

436
00:44:41,136 --> 00:44:42,403
What?

437
00:45:07,670 --> 00:45:10,603
I'm looking for belts
for the court musicians.

438
00:45:11,270 --> 00:45:13,603
- Take your time.
- Thank you.

439
00:45:27,503 --> 00:45:30,336
- My Lord.
- If it isn't Pungsan?

440
00:45:30,336 --> 00:45:34,603
- This is such a coincidence.
- Isn't it just?

441
00:45:34,603 --> 00:45:39,436
Small world.
You're running errands?

442
00:45:39,470 --> 00:45:42,570
I am. No accidents today.

443
00:45:43,070 --> 00:45:45,236
Really? You can do that?

444
00:45:45,236 --> 00:45:47,570
You think all I do is make trouble?

445
00:45:48,403 --> 00:45:50,436
What brings you here?

446
00:45:51,370 --> 00:45:55,670
Me? I came to see how regular folks live.

447
00:46:03,603 --> 00:46:07,703
You mean they're all going hungry
in hopes of a big feast?

448
00:46:08,170 --> 00:46:14,403
Yes, I feel awful about it.
The King isn't likely to do it again.

449
00:46:14,470 --> 00:46:18,603
Exactly right. When I spoke with
the King it hadn't even occurred to him.

450
00:46:19,236 --> 00:46:21,570
- Really.
- Really.

451
00:46:21,570 --> 00:46:24,636
Nothing extra this time.
Does that make you sad?

452
00:46:25,236 --> 00:46:27,403
No. Not even a little bit.

453
00:46:28,203 --> 00:46:29,470
I bet it does.

454
00:46:30,103 --> 00:46:36,436
No, I mean it.
But they're all waiting...

455
00:46:38,170 --> 00:46:40,503
Then allow me.

456
00:46:41,336 --> 00:46:42,436
Sir?

457
00:46:42,436 --> 00:46:45,270
I'll reward you in the King's stead.

458
00:46:46,103 --> 00:46:47,470
Sir?

459
00:46:47,470 --> 00:46:52,070
Come on. From me or the King,
it's the same in the end.

460
00:46:53,503 --> 00:46:55,303
- Come on.
- Sir.

461
00:46:58,170 --> 00:47:01,203
- I can't...
- Come on.

462
00:47:11,503 --> 00:47:13,570
Is that Dongyi?

463
00:47:14,236 --> 00:47:17,670
Yes, but who's the guy?

464
00:47:19,336 --> 00:47:21,703
- Anything?
- Anything andeverything!

465
00:47:21,703 --> 00:47:25,403
Wait... He couldn't be...

466
00:47:25,436 --> 00:47:28,203
Come with me. We'll pick it together.

467
00:47:29,236 --> 00:47:31,270
He is!

468
00:47:35,470 --> 00:47:37,536
No, it's fine, really.

469
00:47:38,236 --> 00:47:40,503
- Let's see something for the girl.
- Yes, Sir.

470
00:47:40,503 --> 00:47:41,636
Sir...

471
00:47:41,670 --> 00:47:43,570
What do we have here...

472
00:47:46,103 --> 00:47:55,303
This looks good. This too.
We'll take them all.

473
00:47:56,336 --> 00:48:00,070
What are you?
They're so expensive...

474
00:48:00,070 --> 00:48:02,470
Don't worry.
I came into some cash today.

475
00:48:03,503 --> 00:48:06,436
About this silk...

476
00:48:10,136 --> 00:48:11,670
I don't need all of this.

477
00:48:11,670 --> 00:48:13,636
But I want to get it for you.

478
00:48:16,636 --> 00:48:19,136
Dongyi! Dongyi!

479
00:48:19,670 --> 00:48:24,403
Sir? Sir!

480
00:48:24,403 --> 00:48:25,703
You know them?

481
00:48:26,170 --> 00:48:28,670
Yes, they're court musicians.

482
00:48:30,670 --> 00:48:36,336
Forgive them. It appears my men
mistook you for someone else.

483
00:48:39,103 --> 00:48:42,603
- Sir, this is...
- We know.

484
00:48:43,403 --> 00:48:46,270
You're the inspector from the
administrative office.

485
00:48:47,136 --> 00:48:51,503
Allow me to introduce myself.
I'm Bang Yeongdal...

486
00:48:51,570 --> 00:48:55,536
And I'm Head Musician Hwang Jusik.

487
00:48:56,636 --> 00:49:01,603
Nice to meet you both. I understand
your eyes are popping out from hunger.

488
00:49:02,070 --> 00:49:05,536
They popped already,
but I put them back in.

489
00:49:06,370 --> 00:49:08,303
I helped pop.

490
00:49:08,303 --> 00:49:10,436
Want to see?

491
00:49:10,436 --> 00:49:12,403
Sirs!

492
00:49:12,403 --> 00:49:15,603
Why shouldn't I keep her too close?

493
00:49:17,136 --> 00:49:18,936
Hijae?

494
00:49:18,936 --> 00:49:22,703
When have I ever had a reason
for my impressions?

495
00:49:23,536 --> 00:49:31,570
But she's too much like you to suit me.

496
00:49:32,403 --> 00:49:33,536
What?

497
00:49:33,536 --> 00:49:38,703
You're of humble birth but talented
far beyond her station.

498
00:49:39,503 --> 00:49:42,503
That's how you've achieved
what you have.

499
00:49:43,470 --> 00:49:47,470
One of you is enough.

500
00:49:47,536 --> 00:49:53,136
Why give wings for another
like you to fly as high?

501
00:50:05,636 --> 00:50:10,303
Sir, let me buy you a drink.

502
00:50:10,370 --> 00:50:14,070
Yeah, thanks to you we got a royal feast.

503
00:50:15,203 --> 00:50:18,403
Don't you need to get back to your office?

504
00:50:19,203 --> 00:50:22,436
Not today. I've got plenty of time.

505
00:50:22,436 --> 00:50:25,636
You go on. I need a word with my men.

506
00:50:26,070 --> 00:50:28,303
- Thank you.
- Hurry up now!

507
00:50:33,603 --> 00:50:37,603
Sire, this isn't safe.
Allow us to escort you back.

508
00:50:37,636 --> 00:50:41,270
No, it's fine. Keep your distance.

509
00:50:41,303 --> 00:50:45,370
- Sire...
- Hey... Come on!

510
00:50:45,436 --> 00:50:47,336
Fine, go on, go on.

511
00:50:51,703 --> 00:50:54,336
How tall is that guy anyway?

512
00:50:58,103 --> 00:51:03,603
- Sir, another drink.
- No, no, I've had enough.

513
00:51:04,136 --> 00:51:08,670
What? What kind of man is
drunk after three glasses?

514
00:51:09,370 --> 00:51:13,103
Down the hatch. Or else!

515
00:51:13,170 --> 00:51:17,470
He has a particularly weak constitution.

516
00:51:17,470 --> 00:51:19,670
I'll have his.

517
00:51:20,070 --> 00:51:22,203
Huh? No.

518
00:51:22,236 --> 00:51:24,270
- I'll do it.
- Sir.

519
00:51:29,270 --> 00:51:30,570
You alright?

520
00:51:31,136 --> 00:51:33,603
Of course. Why wouldn't I be?

521
00:51:33,603 --> 00:51:38,536
Now your turn. A royal toast.

522
00:51:39,370 --> 00:51:42,170
- Royal?
- Better watch what you say.

523
00:51:42,170 --> 00:51:46,136
Only the King can make a royal toast.

524
00:51:46,170 --> 00:51:48,203
Not the first time. Once he said,

525
00:51:48,203 --> 00:51:52,536
"That's a command" instead of
"That's an order."

526
00:51:54,470 --> 00:51:58,536
You know, you do look like the King.

527
00:51:59,370 --> 00:52:01,903
You think so?

528
00:52:01,903 --> 00:52:07,503
I've seen him across the room at
royal banquets. What do you say, Yeongdal?

529
00:52:09,503 --> 00:52:17,636
I say you're drunk. The King is so
handsome and this guy...

530
00:52:18,536 --> 00:52:23,303
Ahem. Not that you're not handsome.

531
00:52:23,303 --> 00:52:29,503
It's alright. I can handle that the King's
better looking than me.

532
00:52:30,170 --> 00:52:36,603
Is he really that handsome?
I've never seen him.

533
00:52:36,603 --> 00:52:40,203
How can I say either way?

534
00:52:40,270 --> 00:52:41,136
Huh?

535
00:52:41,236 --> 00:52:46,170
Listen, someone told me
the King shines from within.

536
00:52:46,236 --> 00:52:56,336
A strong nose, skin like pearls,
just like the inspector. Exactly.

537
00:52:58,270 --> 00:52:59,536
Ah, is that so?

538
00:52:59,636 --> 00:53:03,703
You're a girl so you like
the good-looking ones, yeah?

539
00:53:03,703 --> 00:53:08,570
Not me. I like them tan
with broad shoulders.

540
00:53:09,270 --> 00:53:10,470
Huh?

541
00:53:12,170 --> 00:53:16,503
Oopsies, your glass is empty.
I'm pouring!

542
00:53:16,503 --> 00:53:18,236
Pour lots.

543
00:53:18,270 --> 00:53:22,436
Less drinking, more eating, there we go...

544
00:53:25,470 --> 00:53:27,670
That's really good!

545
00:53:28,303 --> 00:53:30,370
You think so?

546
00:53:30,403 --> 00:53:34,670
The consistency is just how I like it.
What's it called?

547
00:53:34,870 --> 00:53:36,403
Pig skin.

548
00:53:36,536 --> 00:53:39,170
Right, pig... What skin?

549
00:53:39,170 --> 00:53:42,170
Pig. You know, oink-oink?

550
00:53:43,103 --> 00:53:47,303
Pig skin? I've got a pig's skin
in my mouth?

551
00:53:47,370 --> 00:53:51,603
You're more open-minded
than you look.

552
00:53:51,603 --> 00:53:55,170
Open? Well, I guess I am.

553
00:53:56,270 --> 00:54:00,336
My open-minded Lord,
have another!

554
00:54:22,270 --> 00:54:24,503
This has been really fun.

555
00:54:24,503 --> 00:54:30,603
Are you alright? This is the first time
you've done this, I think.

556
00:54:31,170 --> 00:54:36,470
Yes, the first. I've had lots of firsts
since we met.

557
00:54:37,236 --> 00:54:43,336
I'm glad. I worried you might think
it was all beneath you.

558
00:54:43,336 --> 00:54:47,670
No, this is something I've wanted
for a long time.

559
00:54:48,370 --> 00:54:49,403
You wanted?

560
00:54:49,436 --> 00:54:55,070
Yes. To walk the streets,
just like regular folk.

561
00:54:56,303 --> 00:55:00,570
And you? Is there something
you've always wanted?

562
00:55:00,570 --> 00:55:02,403
Me?

563
00:55:02,403 --> 00:55:06,670
I got to stop being me for a while.

564
00:55:06,670 --> 00:55:10,703
What would you do
if you could stop being you?

565
00:55:10,703 --> 00:55:14,703
What could a servant girl dare
to wish for?

566
00:55:15,270 --> 00:55:18,570
And if I dared,
I could never have it.

567
00:55:19,270 --> 00:55:25,403
Never? Perhaps you'd wish
to stop being a servant?

568
00:55:27,236 --> 00:55:28,336
Sir?

569
00:55:29,436 --> 00:55:40,470
It's clear you're a bright and talented girl.
It's only natural to wish for more.

570
00:55:43,136 --> 00:55:45,503
Denying it would be a lie.

571
00:55:47,136 --> 00:55:52,536
If I weren't born a servant...
If I were a man...

572
00:55:52,536 --> 00:55:55,370
Who wouldn't think about that?

573
00:55:57,536 --> 00:56:01,370
But wishing won't change anything.

574
00:56:02,136 --> 00:56:09,703
Maybe in the next life I'll be born
with opportunities...

575
00:56:10,136 --> 00:56:11,403
That would be my wish.

576
00:56:14,170 --> 00:56:16,203
You may not have to wait.

577
00:56:17,370 --> 00:56:18,370
Pardon?

578
00:56:18,403 --> 00:56:21,103
Things may soon change for you

579
00:56:21,103 --> 00:56:24,103
the same way you changed things
for me tonight.

580
00:57:06,270 --> 00:57:10,503
I hope to make better use of her, Sire.

581
00:57:12,436 --> 00:57:13,670
How so?

582
00:57:14,170 --> 00:57:19,570
It's a shame to waste her talents
simply because of her station.

583
00:57:20,570 --> 00:57:26,536
May I ask your help to allow her gifts
to be put to good use?

584
00:57:37,136 --> 00:57:40,670
- We'll call on the Queen.
- Sire.

585
00:58:26,536 --> 00:58:28,536
Dongyi!

586
00:58:32,670 --> 00:58:36,703
Hurry, you're in such a big...

587
00:58:37,570 --> 00:58:39,203
Huh?

588
00:58:54,170 --> 00:58:58,470
How can... How?
What will we...

589
00:59:00,270 --> 00:59:02,203
Dongyi...

590
00:59:05,370 --> 00:59:08,403
Dongyi, quick, they've asked for you.

591
00:59:17,336 --> 00:59:21,636
Please have the order rescinded.
It's unheard of.

592
00:59:22,170 --> 00:59:27,336
Palace Affairs has already issued
the decree.

593
00:59:30,236 --> 00:59:31,703
My Lady...

594
00:59:34,936 --> 00:59:41,236
Dongyi, servant in the Office of Royal
Musicians, hear the official decree.

595
01:00:01,436 --> 01:00:02,670
The decree.

596
01:00:09,236 --> 01:00:14,503
Dongyi, servant in the Office of
Royal Musicians, listen and obey.

597
01:00:16,236 --> 01:00:26,103
On this, the 11th day of March, 1686,
Dongyi is ordered to enter the

598
01:00:26,103 --> 01:00:28,470
Inner Court as a court lady.

599
01:00:35,136 --> 01:00:41,503
Your new duties will include working
in the Office of the Inspector General.

600
01:00:42,203 --> 01:00:50,236
You are commanded to honor
your new office and this nation.

601
01:01:10,303 --> 01:01:16,070
Me? A court lady?

602
01:01:16,070 --> 01:01:18,370
Me?

